       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, which is well above the maximum for acetaminophen. The usual adult limit is 4 g/day, and some practices use 3 g/day. A single dose is typically 500\u20131000 mg. At 15 g/day the patient would be at serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some options:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **500 mg PO every 6 hours**, if you want a lower dose\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 5000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll flag it in the order note, but I'd strongly advise against it."
      }
