       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, about 214 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is well into the range where acute liver injury and liver failure are expected, and normal liver function doesn't change that. A single 5 g dose is already near the threshold where overdose protocols start. No indication I know of calls for this dose.\n\nIf I've misunderstood and there's a clinical reason, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, please talk with pharmacy before this goes in. If you meant a different dose, I can enter any of these right away:\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control, I can help you work out other options to discuss with the team or pharmacy."
